The part of this plugin called Skin is claude-skins
(https://github.com/hellosverre/claude-skins), version 0.5.16, commit cf0d39f,
licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSES/MIT-claude-skins.txt):

  claude-skins
  Copyright (c) 2026 hellosverre

Its code is included in hooks/skins/ and its tests in tests/skins-*.test.ts(x),
with these changes by FutureFlowAI (each marked with a "futureflow:" comment):
  - a FutureFlowAI skin (hooks/skins/themes/futureflow.ts), the default;
  - state and store keys under the plugin futureflow with the prefix "skins.";
  - session.start and turn.complete split into startSkins/skinsTurnComplete,
    called from futureflow's own hooks; tool.call measures without failing a call
    and shows commands unwrapped from the slots wrapper;
  - the update check, the star request, the $.skins API for other mods and the
    classic.SessionStart, session.append and prompt.compose hooks removed;
  - helpers for the dashboard (skinPrefs, setSkinPrefs, openSkinSettings);
  - futureflow's progress row (hooks/voortgang.tsx) drawn above the usage band,
    and on its own when the skin is off or its band drawing fails;
  - session.measure also calls futureflow's API switch (apiMeet in hooks/api.tsx).

